  "decision": "exclude",
  "confidence": 0.9,
  "reason": "The abstract describes the creation of a cross-species kidney atlas and a computational tool (CellSpectra) to analyze gene expression coordination. While it mentions facilitating the selection of rodent models that reflect human signatures and applying the approach for potential therapeutic selection, it does not report any quantitative measure of agreement (e.g., concordance rate, PPV, sensitivity/specificity) between animal and human results. The focus is on the methodology and atlas creation, not on quantifying the translational accuracy."
